{
	chapter.1F66B030D96EB9E2.chapter_subtitle: ["The Ashborn still has to eat. Last Light feeds itself."]
	chapter.1F66B030D96EB9E2.title: "&aHearth & Harvest"
	quest.069692FDDF270544.quest_desc: [
		"Craft an &6Iron Fishing Rod&r. Aquaculture's rods take a &6hook&r, &6bait&r, a coloured line and a bobber; fit them at a &6Tackle Box&r."
		""
		"Every water keeps its own fish: rivers, oceans, jungles, swamps and frozen seas."
	]
	quest.069692FDDF270544.quest_subtitle: "Fish don't care what happened to the sun."
	quest.069692FDDF270544.title: "A Line in Dark Water"
	quest.1378690974492D71.quest_desc: [
		"Plated meals grant &6Nourishment&r: your hunger stops draining while it lasts. Soups and stews grant &6Comfort&r: you heal naturally however empty your stomach is."
		""
		"Eat one before a long dungeon and you won't be chewing bread in the middle of a boss's second phase."
	]
	quest.1378690974492D71.quest_subtitle: "A full belly outlasts a long fight."
	quest.1378690974492D71.title: "Nourishing!"
	quest.1BA27B12A75053E1.quest_desc: [
		"Knot &6Fishing Nets&r from string, then a &6Crab Pot&r from nets and sticks, or buy one from a coast fisherman. Set it in open water with &6bait&r inside."
		""
		"&6Fish Bait&r is seeds and rotten flesh. &6Chum&r and &6Glow Bait&r are the others; the swamp folk swear by chum. Rain doubles the catch, and a hopper underneath empties the pot for you."
	]
	quest.1BA27B12A75053E1.quest_subtitle: "Bait it, sink it, walk away."
	quest.1BA27B12A75053E1.title: "Pot Luck"
	quest.267A34C74D5C4387.quest_desc: [
		"Cook a &6feast&r (a Roast Chicken, a Stuffed Pumpkin, a Honey Glazed Ham or a Shepherd's Pie) and set it down. Anyone with a bowl can take a serving."
		""
		"The sellswords of the Ashen Company will fight for gold. They'll stay for this."
	]
	quest.267A34C74D5C4387.quest_subtitle: "Some meals are meant for the whole village."
	quest.267A34C74D5C4387.title: "&aA Glorious Feast"
	quest.26F13D2CFD0BD33F.quest_desc: [
		"Brew plain &6beer&r first: water, wheat, seeds and a brown mushroom. Then ferment that beer again with beetroot, potato, another mushroom and a strip of &6jerky&r."
		""
		"&6Strongroot Ale&r is a miner's drink. It makes a long day underground feel shorter, and the walk home feel longer."
	]
	quest.26F13D2CFD0BD33F.quest_subtitle: "Beer, improved by things that grow underground."
	quest.26F13D2CFD0BD33F.title: "Strongroot Ale"
	quest.27B8119DAEAD1FB1.quest_desc: [
		"Visit all seven: the Cottage, the Harbour Pier, the Lighthouse, the Stilt Shack, the Ice Fishing Camp, the River Boathouse and, under twelve blocks of water, the &6Sunken Trawler&r."
		""
		"&7The captain's chest on the trawler sometimes holds a Heart of the Sea. The drowned deckhands would rather it didn't."
	]
	quest.27B8119DAEAD1FB1.quest_subtitle: "Seven places on the water."
	quest.27B8119DAEAD1FB1.title: "&aCoastal Wanderer"
	quest.2CB0F847FFAEAE21.quest_desc: [
		"Build a &6Stove&r from bricks, iron and a campfire, and set a &6Cooking Pot&r on it. Any heat beneath will do; the stove just does it with dignity."
		""
		"The pot takes up to six ingredients and a bowl, and gives back meals that keep you going far longer than raw meat ever did."
		""
		"&o\"A shrine warms the dead. A stove warms the living. Keep both lit.\"&r"
	]
	quest.2CB0F847FFAEAE21.quest_subtitle: "A stove, a pot, a reason to come home."
	quest.2CB0F847FFAEAE21.title: "&aDinner's Served"
	quest.322940C8C88BF0BD.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Keg&r (iron, planks and a honeycomb) ferments drinks and cheese from a base liquid and up to four ingredients. Pour from it into &6tankards&r."
		""
		"Some brews want warmth, some want cold. A &6Heating Cask&r or an &6Ice Crate&r next to the keg shifts its temperature."
		""
		"&o\"The Company says it can't fight sober. I've seen it fight drunk. Brew anyway.\"&r"
	]
	quest.322940C8C88BF0BD.quest_subtitle: "Patience, in a barrel."
	quest.322940C8C88BF0BD.title: "Here Starts the Process"
	quest.38273B3664CCA777.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Fisherman's Cottage&r sits on a sandy or snowy beach. Saylor lives there, and trades things no village fisherman will."
		""
		"The coast has six more places like it, each with its own resident: Harbourmaster Wren, Keeper Morrow, Old Bayou Tam, Frost-Beard Ole, Ferryman Hale… and two deckhands who don't say much anymore."
	]
	quest.38273B3664CCA777.quest_subtitle: "Someone on the shore kept fishing through the end of the world."
	quest.38273B3664CCA777.title: "Home of Saylor"
	quest.42FE195A97F774D8.quest_desc: [
		"Land a &6Tuna&r from the open ocean and a &6Catfish&r from a river or lake inland."
		""
		"Fillet the big ones with a &6Fillet Knife&r. A tuna feeds a table. A catfish feeds the village cats, mostly."
	]
	quest.42FE195A97F774D8.quest_subtitle: "Every fisher has a story. Bring proof."
	quest.42FE195A97F774D8.title: "The Ones That Didn't Get Away"
	quest.5316B4764FFB7FDC.quest_desc: [
		"The wild keeps its own larder: &6venison&r from deer, &6drumsticks&r from turkeys, &6duck&r from the ponds, &6crab meat&r on the beaches."
		""
		"Deer bolt at the first footstep. Come at them slowly, or bring a bow."
	]
	quest.5316B4764FFB7FDC.quest_subtitle: "The deer survived the Eclipse. Mostly by running."
	quest.5316B4764FFB7FDC.title: "Game in the Ash"
	quest.54BEC32A2A59D661.quest_desc: [
		"Hold a &6Skillet&r in one hand and raw food in the other, stand near a fire, and cook as you go. Sneak to set it down as a block over a fire or a stove, and it cooks there too."
		""
		"It also makes a perfectly respectable club. Nobody has to know."
	]
	quest.54BEC32A2A59D661.quest_subtitle: "Supper on the road."
	quest.54BEC32A2A59D661.title: "Portable Cooking"
	quest.582A451645F1551B.quest_desc: [
		"You can't die for good. You can still go hungry, and a hungry Ashborn can't sprint, can't heal and can't outrun much of anything."
		""
		"Craft a &6knife&r from flint or iron. It takes more from the world than a sword does: straw from grass, ham from pigs, slices from a fish."
		""
		"&o\"The villages that lived through the Eclipse learned one thing before swordplay. Supper.\"&r"
	]
	quest.582A451645F1551B.quest_subtitle: "Undying isn't the same as fed."
	quest.582A451645F1551B.title: "&aHunt and Gather"
	quest.5C4120A5CBCF549B.quest_desc: [
		"Now and then a rod or a crab pot brings up a &6Message in a Bottle&r. Open it. Some hold a little treasure; some hold a &6Bottled Map to a Wreck&r."
		""
		"The sea had a lot to say before the Eclipse. It hasn't stopped."
	]
	quest.5C4120A5CBCF549B.quest_subtitle: "Twelve notes from the sea. Most of them are complaints."
	quest.5C4120A5CBCF549B.title: "Message Received"
	quest.639D8FCB83578040.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Farming Crate&r harvests, replants and stores everything in the 9×9 around it, and never voids a harvest."
		""
		"Set one in the middle of the village fields and go kill something. Supper will be waiting."
	]
	quest.639D8FCB83578040.quest_subtitle: "Let the box do the stooping."
	quest.639D8FCB83578040.title: "The Crate That Farms"
	quest.65CD1B65F3364DF4.quest_desc: [
		"Cut grass, wheat or rice with your knife and keep the &6straw&r."
		""
		"Straw twists into rope and canvas. Rope climbs, and tomatoes climb it too. Canvas keeps the rain off the larder."
	]
	quest.65CD1B65F3364DF4.quest_subtitle: "Nothing in a village goes to waste."
	quest.65CD1B65F3364DF4.title: "Grasping at Straws"
	quest.685BB5F97A1C8228.quest_desc: [
		"Mix &6Organic Compost&r from dirt, straw, bone meal and rotten flesh (or tree bark), set it down and leave it be. Sunlight, water and nearby mushrooms hurry it along."
		""
		"In time it turns into &6Rich Soil&r. Crops grown in it get a free push now and then, and mushrooms planted on it spread into colonies."
		""
		"&7The dead feed the living. Even here."
	]
	quest.685BB5F97A1C8228.quest_subtitle: "Rot, patience, then something green."
	quest.685BB5F97A1C8228.title: "Plant Food"
	quest.69446A3F5A0ACE55.quest_desc: [
		"Wild &6cabbages&r, &6tomatoes&r, &6onions&r and &6rice&r still grow where farms stood before the Eclipse: on beaches, in the warm grasslands, along the rivers. Village farms sometimes keep a row of them."
		""
		"Gather any of them and bring the seed home."
	]
	quest.69446A3F5A0ACE55.quest_subtitle: "Somebody planted these, once."
	quest.69446A3F5A0ACE55.title: "Crops of the Wild"
	quest.6CB9503B1FD8393F.quest_desc: [
		"On a stony shore stands a &6Lighthouse&r. Keeper Morrow lives there, and trades with anyone who makes the climb."
		""
		"&o\"A keeper of a light, by the sea. We'd have a great deal to talk about, he and I.\"&r"
	]
	quest.6CB9503B1FD8393F.quest_subtitle: "Another fire someone refused to let go out."
	quest.6CB9503B1FD8393F.title: "Keeper of the Light"
	quest.6F9D0921E45DDD1A.quest_desc: [
		"Right-click a ripe crop to harvest and replant it in one motion. With a hoe in hand the harvest sweeps: iron or gold 3×3, diamond 5×5."
		""
		"A &6Sprinkler&r (copper and a bucket) keeps a 9×9 field wet and growing about three times as fast. It needs water within four blocks, below it or beside it."
	]
	quest.6F9D0921E45DDD1A.quest_subtitle: "The sky stopped helping. Copper didn't."
	quest.6F9D0921E45DDD1A.title: "Rain on Demand"
	quest.726D1A034A7B4C5F.quest_desc: [
		"Eat a course of every meal the cooking pot knows. It's a long menu. You have, technically, forever."
		""
		"&7A long-term goal. Your advancements list the dishes you still owe."
	]
	quest.726D1A034A7B4C5F.quest_subtitle: "Every dish, at least once."
	quest.726D1A034A7B4C5F.title: "Master of the Last Kitchen"
	quest.736B14FDA7FC812D.quest_desc: [
		"Plant &6rice&r in water one block deep. It grows up out of the water and gives you grain and straw both."
		""
		"Half the cooking pot's recipes start with rice. The other half want an onion."
	]
	quest.736B14FDA7FC812D.quest_subtitle: "Rice wants its feet wet."
	quest.736B14FDA7FC812D.title: "Dipping Your Roots"
	quest.739A57228824E136.quest_desc: [
		"Ferment milk with a brown mushroom, pumpkin seeds and sugar in a &6warm&r keg. Draw the full keg off with a &6honeycomb&r for a rind and you get an &6Unripe Cheese Wheel&r. Set it down and leave it alone."
		""
		"When it's ripe, cut it into wedges on a board. Cheese keeps. Most things in this world don't."
	]
	quest.739A57228824E136.quest_subtitle: "The one thing here that improves with age."
	quest.739A57228824E136.title: "Taste of Time"
	quest.7412822E46239020.quest_desc: [
		"Fill a keg with honey, add wheat, seeds and sweet berries, and wait. &6Mead&r is what the Ashen Company drinks to its dead."
		""
		"Every brew leaves you a little &6Tipsy&r. Don't roll into a fight seeing double."
	]
	quest.7412822E46239020.quest_subtitle: "Honey, wheat and sweet berries. And time."
	quest.7412822E46239020.title: "Mead for the Living"
	quest.7F2214D371459953.quest_desc: [
		"Place a &6Cutting Board&r, set an item on it and use it with a tool in hand. A knife slices meat, fish and vegetables; an axe strips logs and keeps the bark."
		""
		"More food from less. That's the whole trick of surviving."
	]
	quest.7F2214D371459953.quest_subtitle: "Steel for the monsters. A board for the meat."
	quest.7F2214D371459953.title: "Watch Your Fingers"
}
